QuestGuidance.Register("en",151,{
[4801]="700442D5\n1\tDefeat Ughâsh the Unslakable\tDefeat Ughâsh the Unslakable before its flames overwhelm the defenders of Minas Tirith.\n",
[4802]="7006943D\n1\tCraft a crate of cooked food for the Umbar Cook's Guild\tThe recipe needed to complete this quest is available for purchase. Purchase the quest recipe from the guild leader. Create a crate of cooked food for Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tDeliver a crate of food to the Umbar Cook's Guild Leader\tProvide the cooked plates to the Umbar Cook's Guild Leader.\n",
[4803]="7006B108\n1\tCraft a crate of cooked food for the Umbar Cook's Guild\tThe recipe needed to complete this quest is available for purchase. Purchase the quest recipe from the guild leader. Create a crate of cooked food for Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tDeliver a crate of food to the Umbar Cook's Guild Leader\tProvide the cooked plates to the Umbar Cook's Guild Leader.\n",
[4804]="700683D1\n1\tCollect sea-hawk eggs from nests ([see journal]/14)\tNorth, beyond Umbar city, where the hills roll into the shore, sea-hawks soar above the land. They build nests in the crags and trees. They lay eggs prized by the chefs of Umbar. Collect the eggs and return to Luthana at the expedition camp.\n2\tYour efforts to collect sea-hawk eggs proved fruitful. All you need do now is return your precious cargo to Luthana at the hunter's expedition in the south-eastern portion of the Cape of Umbar.\t\n",
[4805]="7006EAE0\n1\tEnter the Apothecary of Dâr Tabib in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl\tThe Apothecary of Dâr Tabib is located in the Tor-gardens of Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tTalk to Corudan in Dâr Tabib\tCorudan lies in one of the beds of Dâr Tabib.\n3\tTalk to Sigileth in Dâr Tabib\tSigileth watches over her brother in Dâr Tabib.\n4\tTalk to Sigileth in Dâr Tabib and hear her account of their return to the city\tSigileth is in Dâr Tabib.\n5\tTalk to Sigileth in Dâr Tabib\tSigileth is in Dâr Tabib.\n6\tTalk to Caebar in Dâr Tabib\tCaebar is in Dâr Tabib.\n7\tTalk to Sigileth in Dâr Tabib\tSigileth is in Dâr Tabib.\n8\tRetrieve Corudan's notes about the Fearwater from the satchel at the foot of his bed\tCorudan's possessions can be found in the satchel at the foot of his bed.\n9\tBring Corudan's notes to Caebar in Dâr Tabib\tCaebar is in Dâr Tabib.\n10\tTalk to Caebar in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr Tabib\tCaebar waits for you in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr Tabib.\n11\tWait for Caebar to speak again\tCaebar thinks for a moment about what you have shown him.\n12\tTalk to Caebar in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr Tabib\tCaebar stands in the Tor-gardens outside Dâr Tabib.\n",
[4806]="70042885\n1\tDefeat Amardam\tAmardam can be found somewhere in the Duvuinen Swamp. You should awake and defeat Amardam.\n2\tSpeak with Cánnakh\tCánnakh can be found in Aughaire. You should speak with Cánnakh.\n",
[4807]="70053B22\n1\tFind someone who knows about the broken key\tYou must find someone who knows what the broken key might once have unlocked. But who could hold that secret?\n2\tGive the broken key to Khîl Tale-spinner in the hidden chamber\tIs it possible that Khîl Tale-spinner might know something about the broken key given to you by Gothmog?\n3\tTalk to a metalworker by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast\tMetalworkers can be found on the lower level of Járnfast.\n4\tTalk to Khîl Tale-spinner by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast\tKhîl Tale-spinner is by the forges in Járnfast.\n5\tGive the mould to the metalworker by the forges in Járnfast\tThe metalworkers are by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast.\n6\tWait for the metalworker to forge a key using the mould\tThe metalworker needs some time to fashion a new key using the mould provided by Khîl Tale-spinner.\n7\tTalk to the metalworker by the forges in Járnfast\tThe metalworker is by the forges on the lower level of Járnfast. He should have finished forging the key by now.\n8\tTalk to Khîl in the hidden chamber in his home\tKhîl Tale-spinner has returned to the hidden chamber built by his thrice-great grandfather Vóin.\n9\tUnlock the tiny locked box in the hidden chamber\tKhîl told you about a tiny locked box that he thought his mother used to store jewels, but perhaps it is far older than that... He has placed it on the table in the hidden chamber, and waits for you to try the newly-forged key in its lock.\n10\tTalk to Khîl in the hidden chamber in his home\tKhîl Tale-spinner is in the hidden chamber built by his thrice-great grandfather Vóin.\n11\tBring the glass shard to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús\tGandalf intended to travel north with the casket containing the bones of Isildur, and should have arrived at the Beorninghús by now. You should bring him the glass shard you found within the tiny locked box from Khîl's home.\n",
[4808]="70054717\n1\tDeliver the Black Book to Khîl Tale-spinner in his home\030Deliver the Black Book to Covadil in the Houses of Lore\030Deliver the Black Book to Karazgar by the flat stone at the Old Ford\tGandalf has presented you with a choice concerning the ultimate disposition of the Black Book of Mordor.\n2\tGandalf gave you the choice of where to bring the Black Book and you have now performed that duty.\t\n",
[4809]="70059B11\n1\tReturn to Mótsog's Tomb at the bottom of the secret stair beneath Zul-mazal\tThe entrance to the secret stair that leads to Mótsog's Tomb, deep below Gundabad, is in Zul-mazal.\n2\tWait for Durin to arrive\tDurin hurries to Mótsog's Tomb to speak with the last of the Greymauls before the day comes to an end.\n3\tTalk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb\tDurin has come to Mótsog's Tomb to speak with the last of the Greymauls before the day is ended.\n4\tTalk to Mótsog and hear his response\tDurin has come to Mótsog's Tomb to speak with the last of the Greymauls before the day is ended.\n5\tTalk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb\tDurin is in Mótsog's Tomb, thinking about the words of the last Greymaul.\n6\tExamine the statue of Mótsog\tMótsog is gone, and only a statue remains.\n7\tTalk to Durin in Mótsog's Tomb\tDurin is in Mótsog's Tomb, thinking about the road that brought him here... and the road that still lies ahead.\n",
[4810]="7006EADE\n1\tTalk to Tatháta at Dâr Rapha and consider her words\tTatháta is at Dâr Rapha, outside the city.\n2\tTalk to Tatháta at Dâr Rapha\tTatháta is at Dâr Rapha, outside the city.\n3\tTalk to Daxamat at Dâr Rapha\tDaxamat is at Dâr Rapha, outside the city.\n",
[4811]="70053B27\n1\tTalk to the shade of Isildur by the waggon in Laerlad\tThe shade of Isildur is by the waggon bearing his bones northward, in Laerlad.\n2\tThe shade of Tárandil fades from view\tThe shade of Tárandil has made his decision: he will seek out Bravantel and Héol, no matter the torment it will cause him.\n3\tTalk to Gandalf by the waggon in Laerlad\tGandalf is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward, in Laerlad.\n4\tMeet up with Gandalf and the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur at the entrance to the valley of Rivendell\tGandalf suggested you catch up with the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur when it arrives at the entrance to the valley of Rivendell.\n5\tTalk to the shade of Isildur at the entrance to Rivendell\tThe shade of Isildur has at last finished the journey he swore in life to undertake more than three thousand years ago.\n6\tThe shade of Isildur fades from view\tThe shade of Isildur has at last finished the journey he swore in life to undertake more than three thousand years ago.\n7\tTalk to Gandalf by the waggon near the entrance to Rivendell\tGandalf is by the waggon bearing Isildur's bones to Rivendell, by the entrance to that secret valley.\n8\tTalk to Gandalf by the entrance to Rivendell and complete 'Instance: Freed of the Burden'\tGandalf is by the waggon bearing Isildur's bones to Rivendell, by the entrance to that secret valley. He has finished reading the secret writing in the Black Book of Mordor, and wishes to tell you the end of that tale.\n9\tTalk to Gandalf by the waggon near the entrance to Rivendell\tGandalf is by the waggon bearing Isildur's bones to Rivendell, by the entrance to that secret valley.\n",
[4812]="70053B25\n1\tTalk to the shade of Tárandil and complete 'Instance: His Father's Son'\tThe shade of Tárandil is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.\n2\tTalk to Gandalf by the waggon in Laerlad\tGandalf is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.\n",
[4813]="70053B23\n1\tFind the waggon carrying Isildur's bones on the road through Laerlad, beside the Gladden Fields\tThe waggon bearing Isildur's bones is in Laerlad, on the road beside the Gladden Fields.\n2\tTalk to the shade of Isildur beside the waggon in Laerlad\tThe shade of Isildur feels the presence of his bones, and follows with interest their northward course along the river.\n3\tTalk to Gandalf beside the waggon in Laerlad\tGandalf is by the waggon bearing Isildur's bones through Laerlad.\n4\tLook for the source of the dread by the waggon\tGandalf has directed you to look for the source of the dread near the waggon bearing Isildur's bones.\n5\tTalk to Vágari the Wanderer\tVágari the Wanderer has appeared by the waggon. But why has he chosen to appear now?\n6\tTalk to Gandalf by the waggon in Laerlad\tGandalf is by the waggon bearing Isildur's bones, near to the Gladden Fields.\n",
[4814]="70041AEF\n1\tFind and confront Drugât\tDrugât is located somewhere in the caverns of Nimrond. You should find and confront Drugât.\n2\tSpeak with Drugât\tDrugât is located somewhere in the caverns of Nimrond. You should speak with Drugât.\n3\tFind the Second Age Amethyst\030Find the Second Age Ingot\030Find the Second Age Trinket\030Find the Second Age Rune\030Find the Second Age Crown\tTreasures of the Second Age can be found in Western Gondor and the Paths of the Dead. You should seek out the five treasures of the Second Age.\n4\tReturn the Second Age treasures to Drugât\tDrugât is located in the caverns of Nimrond. You should return the Second Age treasures to Drugât.\n",
[4815]="700420F4\n1\tSearch near Hata Kebir for Jajax and Daxamat\tHata Kebir can be found far to the south-east of Ost Anglebed. Nimithil has asked you to seek out Jajax, if he still remains in Lebennin. You should begin your search near Hata Kebir.\n2\tSearch the shores of the Anduin south of Aerthir\tAerthir can be found due south of Ost Anglebed along the shores of the Anduin. You have not found Jajax near Hata Kebir, but you should continue your search along the coast to the south of Aerthir.\n3\tTalk to Jajax\tJajax can be found along the coastline to the south of Aerthir. You have discovered Jajax and Daxamat resting from readying their ship, and should speak to them.\n4\tShare a drink with Jajax and Daxamat\tA bottle of wine can be found in the basket next to Jajax. Jajax has asked you to share a bottle of fine wine with him and Daxamat.\n5\tTalk to Jajax\tJajax can be found along the coastline to the south of Aerthir. You have shared wine with Jajax and should speak to him once more.\n6\tReturn to Nimithil in Ost Anglebed\tNimithil can be found in Ost Anglebed in north-central Lebennin. You found Jajax and Daxamat preparing to sail from Lebennin. You should tell Nimithil of your journey.\n",
[4816]="70053B26\n1\tTalk to the shade of Tárandil and complete 'Instance: The Disaster'\tThe shade of Tárandil is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.\n2\tTalk to the shade of Tárandil by the waggon in Laerlad\tThe shade of Tárandil is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.\n",
[4817]="7006EADC\n1\tFind someone at the Northern Ship-yard who will tell you the situation in the city\tSomeone at the Northern Ship-yard around the corner to the east may have further information for you concerning the political situation in Umbar Baharbêl.\n2\tTalk to Jínen outside the Gate of Songs\tJínen was on her way to the Gate of Songs north of the city.\n3\tMeet the Ghad Imghêda at Dâr Rapha, up the hill to the east\tDâr Rapha is up the hill to the east of the Gate of Songs, outside the city.\n4\tTalk to Jajax at Dâr Rapha\tJajax has come to Dâr Rapha, outside the city.\n5\tThe leaders of the Ghad Imghêda are at Dâr Rapha.\t\n6\tThe leaders of the Ghad Imghêda are at Dâr Rapha.\t\n7\tThe leaders of the Ghad Imghêda are at Dâr Rapha.\t\n8\tThe leaders of the Ghad Imghêda are at Dâr Rapha.\t\n",
[4818]="70053B24\n1\tTalk to Vágari and complete 'Instance: The Wanderer's Confession'\tVágari the Wanderer is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.\n2\tTalk to Gandalf by the waggon in Laerlad\tGandalf is by the waggon bearing the bones of Isildur northward.\n",
[4819]="700420F5\n1\tSeek out Roamingstar in her glade\tRoamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil. Erchar wishes to thank the Maiden of the Gilrain for watching over the people of Central Gondor.\n2\tSearch the banks of the Gilrain for a man\tThe man Roamingstar pulled from the Gilrain can be found along the nearby banks. Roamingstar rescued a man from the waters of the Gilrain and healed his wounds. You should examine the sleeping man.\n3\tTalk to Roamingstar\tRoamingstar can be found in her glade in north-eastern Dor-en-Ernil. You have discovered Garvir sleeping along the river-banks, much to your surprise. You should again speak to Roamingstar.\n4\tTell Erchar of Garvir's return\tErchar can be found in Linhir in eastern Dor-en-Ernil. You have learned that Garvir was saved by the Maiden of the Gilrain as he fell into the river. You should tell Erchar that his brother lives!\n5\tTalk to Garvir\tGarvir can be found in Linhir. Garvir has returned to Linhir, much to his brothers' amazement. You should speak to him, and welcome him home.\n",
[4820]="70059354\n1\tTravel to the meeting between Aran Greenwith and Enid Nettlesting\tAran Greenwith and Enid Nettlesting plan to meet in the centre of the Wildwood. You should travel to the designated meeting location.\n2\tTalk to Enid Nettlesting\tEnid Nettlesting can be found at the meeting location in the Wildwood. You should talk to Enid Nettlesting.\n3\tTalk to Aran Greenwith\tAran Greenwith can be found at the meeting location in the Wildwood. You should talk to Aran Greenwith.\n4\tReturn to Trader's Wharf\030Return to Trestlebridge\tYou should return to either Trestlebridge or Trader's Wharf.\n",
[4821]="7004D097\n1\tFind Draigoch's bones\030Find Thorog's bones with Sigrun's aid\030Find Bregmor's bones with Fotri's aid\tThe dwarf Sigrun can aid you in the Misty Mountains, as can Fotri in Forochel. Draigoch's Lair can be found in Thrór's Coomb in Enedwaith. You should seek the bones of the dragons Bregmor, Draigoch, and Thorog.\n2\tCompleted\tLearned more about Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior.\n",
[4822]="70053B28\n1\tTalk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús and complete 'Instance: Vóin's Tale'\tGandalf is inside the Beorninghús, eager to decipher the secret writing in the Black Book of Mordor.\n2\tTalk to Gandalf inside the Beorninghús\tGandalf is inside the Beorninghús.\n",
[4823]="7003669A\n1\tTalk to JWBarry\tBy completing this quest, you will receive all deeds for Erebor.\n",
